.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-veil-repo-id 1  "git-veil-repo-id " 
.SH NAME
git\-veil\-repo\-id \- Show the repository ID derived from the git remote push URL
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-veil repo\-id\fR [\fB\-\-git\-remote\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the repository ID derived from the git remote push URL
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Prints the repository ID derived from the git remote push URL \- the
exact string trust expects as its repo_id argument (trust re\-derives it
from the remote and refuses a mismatch). Pass \-\-git\-remote if your remote is
not \*(Aqorigin\*(Aq.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-veil repo\-id
  $ git\-veil repo\-id \-\-git\-remote upstream
